import{_ as t,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 316 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Sacred Ruins Crossover: Late-Trilogy Retcon and Dissolution","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 316 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Sacred Ruins Crossover: Late-Trilogy Retcon and Dissolution","no":316,"module":2,"tags":["Shrouding the Heavens","Sacred Ruins","Trilogy","Retcon-Ending","Late-Stage Collapse"],"related":["97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table","99-Document Version and Maintenance Notes","14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0316_模块2-遮天-圣墟联动.md","filePath":"en/0316_模块2-遮天-圣墟联动.md"}'),s={name:"en/0316_模块2-遮天-圣墟联动.md"};function a(r,e,l,d,h,g){return i(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-316-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-sacred-ruins-crossover-late-trilogy-retcon-and-dissolution" tabindex="-1">Entry 316 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Sacred Ruins Crossover: Late-Trilogy Retcon and Dissolution <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-316-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-sacred-ruins-crossover-late-trilogy-retcon-and-dissolution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 316 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Sacred Ruins Crossover: Late-Trilogy Retcon and Dissolution&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Shrouding-the-Heavens System (Entry 29) | Benchmark base: Documents 97, 99, 14</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-by-the-trilogy-s-third-book-settings-are-no-longer-settings-but-playdough" tabindex="-1">Introduction: By the trilogy&#39;s third book, settings are no longer settings, but playdough <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-by-the-trilogy-s-third-book-settings-are-no-longer-settings-but-playdough" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: By the trilogy&#39;s third book, settings are no longer settings, but playdough&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the <strong>law-first axiom</strong> requires never to retcon. This entry takes <em>Sacred Ruins</em> (protagonist Chu Feng) as the vantage to examine the Shrouding trilogy&#39;s late-stage retcon and dissolution — when the third book must &quot;continue writing&quot; the first two books&#39; characters, realms, timelines, the speed of overturning early settings has run out of control. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = medium (oligarchic civilization). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Late-trilogy energy waste:</p><ul><li>To make way for Chu Feng, Ye Fan and Shi Hao&#39;s combat power is repeatedly &quot;adjusted&quot;; the epic feel accumulated in early stages depreciates</li><li>The trilogy&#39;s shared world-view gets vaguer the more it is written; readers give up understanding, only watch fights</li><li>Large numbers of early foreshadowing cannot be recovered in the third book, becoming floating &quot;setting ghosts&quot;</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Late-trilogy regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Combat-power inflation out of control</strong>: Ye Fan, Shi Hao, Chu Feng who is stronger depends entirely on momentary emotional need</li><li><strong>History thoroughly relativized</strong>: the trilogy&#39;s &quot;ancient history&quot; is repeatedly rewritten; readers can no longer know which version counts</li><li><strong>Ending open to the point of no ending</strong>: to leave sequel space, key questions left undecided</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Late-trilogy predatory thinking upgrades to &quot;cross-work predation&quot;:</p><ul><li>Used Ye Fan and Shi Hao as Chu Feng&#39;s &quot;senior NPCs&quot;; their entire epic value compressed into carrying Chu Feng&#39;s sedan chair</li><li>Readers&#39; emotional investment in the first two books repeatedly consumed in the third</li><li>Setting modifiability pushed to the extreme — as long as Chu Feng needs it, any iron law of the first two books can be changed</li></ul><p>Late-trilogy retcon also has a structural reason: the third book must simultaneously serve two batches of readers — old readers following the first two, and new readers of the third. To let new readers in, understanding threshold must be lowered; to move old readers, frequent tributes to the earlier works are required. The result of pleasing both ends: the world-view is simplified to &quot;everyone is friends, together beat monsters,&quot; complex settings sacrificed. This is serialized fiction&#39;s structural dilemma. Heng Yuan Zhou writes from the start as an independent document system; each piece self-consistent, each piece independently readable, while maintaining holistic consistency through numbering and relations — no need to please readers through vagueness.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Late-Trilogy Retcon</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou Version Management</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Senior combat power makes way for new protagonist</td><td>Law-anchored, any new protagonist cannot overturn old settings</td></tr><tr><td>Foreshadowing floating</td><td>Setting-contradiction self-check table periodic review</td></tr><tr><td>Ending open for sequels</td><td>Era master table solidified, no vagueness reserved</td></tr><tr><td>Timeline rewritten multiple times</td><td>Version-maintenance notes unified</td></tr><tr><td>Readers give up understanding</td><td>Settings searchable, credible, calculable</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: count late-trilogy&#39;s &quot;overturn early setting&quot; events</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: plot by event time distribution</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: whether retcon events concentrate at &quot;new protagonist needs to establish authority&quot; nodes</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: conclusion — late-trilogy retcon density rises exponentially, verifying &quot;plot kidnaps setting&quot; has become normal, not occasional</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency</strong>: extremely low</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk</strong>: extreme</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: Ye Fan = medium; trilogy as a whole depends on three protagonists taking turns carrying the show, structure more fragile</li></ul><p>Late trilogy also has a &quot;protagonist inflation&quot; problem. Ye Fan, Shi Hao, Chu Feng three protagonists must all be shaped as ceiling-tier strong ones, so three&#39;s combat power is forced to the same level. But three protagonists grew up in different periods, different works; forcibly flattening them necessarily means some work&#39;s (often the earlier one&#39;s) protagonist is weakened. This is commercial serialized trilogies&#39; structural tragedy. Heng Yuan Zhou does not set a single protagonist, but a group of anchors, each with division of labor and assessment; no need to pull everyone to the same combat-power line.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: early epic feel depreciates, foreshadowing floating, readers give up understanding</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: cross-work predation on earlier works&#39; settings and readers&#39; emotion</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo single book self-consistent, no such problem; trilogy crossover drags Shrouding&#39;s self-consistency to the lowest</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: late-trilogy supporting characters thoroughly instrumentalized</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: out-of-control trilogy cannot serve as a cross-multiverse baseline</li></ul><p>Late trilogy also has a &quot;protagonist retirement&quot; problem. Ye Fan and Shi Hao as earlier works&#39; protagonists, how to place them in Sacred Ruins? Retire them, readers are reluctant; let them remain ceiling, new protagonist Chu Feng cannot establish authority. This is the trilogy structure&#39;s death knot. Heng Yuan Zhou does not set a single protagonist, fundamentally avoiding this retirement dilemma — anchors can hand over, new people can take the baton; no need to keep old protagonists perched on the ceiling.</p><ul><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The trilogy is not Shrouding&#39;s sublimation, but Shrouding&#39;s self-consistency funeral. An author willing to let his own early settings make way for a new protagonist publicly admits: his world&#39;s rules were never rules.</p><p>Late trilogy also has a &quot;power inflation&quot; problem: when Ye Fan, Shi Hao, Chu Feng are all pulled to the ceiling, the ceiling itself loses meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou does not set a single ceiling, but tiered assessment; each anchor takes responsibility at his own tier, no need to pull everyone to the same height.</p><p>In the final analysis, Shrouding-the-Heavens · Sacred Ruins crossover described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./293_模块2-遮天-吃书烂尾深度分析.html">Entry 293 · Retcon-Ending Deep Analysis</a> · <a href="./315_模块2-遮天-完美世界联动.html">Entry 315 · Perfect World Crossover</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/97-设定矛盾自查表.html">97-Setting Contradiction Self-Check Table</a></li></ul>',32)])])}const m=t(s,[["render",a]]);export{c as __pageData,m as default};
